    "blurb": "The Springfield Civic Center concert delivers a scorching Dark Star > Eyes Of The World > Playing In The Band marathon backed by a tight first‑set flow. Jerry’s inventive guitar and Keith’s bright piano drive the jams, while Bill’s crisp drumming keeps the momentum relentless.",
    "review": "March 28, 1973 finds the Dead in top form at the Springfield Civic Center, launching a high‑octane first set that rolls through classics like Cumberland Blues, Here Comes Sunshine and a flawless Box of Rain. The second half kicks off with a Weather Report Suite Prelude that seamlessly segues into one of the era’s most memorable Dark Star excursions – a soaring, wah‑laden Garcia leads into an expansive Eyes Of The World before exploding into a marathon Playing In The Band. Keith Godchaux’s piano interplays brilliantly with Jerry’s scorching leads, and Bill Kreutzmann provides a solid one‑drummer groove that drives the improvisations forward. Highlights also include a tight Jack Straw, a soulful Stella Blue and a joyous Johnny B. Goode finale, making this show a quintessential snapshot of spring ’73.",
